    "q-82061": {
      "dom_id": "step-q82061",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "If $\\overset{―}{X}=\\{p,r,s,w\\}$ and $\\overset{―}{Y}=\\{s,t,v\\},$ then what is $\\overset{―}{X\\cap Y}?$",
      "worked_solution": "De Morgan's law for intersections states that\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{X\\cap Y}≡\\overset{―}{X}\\cup \\overset{―}{Y}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{X\\cap Y} & =\\overset{―}{X}\\cup \\overset{―}{Y} \\\\  & =\\{p,r,s,w\\}\\cup \\{s,t,v\\} \\\\  & =\\{p,r,s,t,v,w\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
