      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "If $\\overset{―}{A}=\\{16,18,26\\}$ and $\\overset{―}{B}=\\{10,16,25\\},$ then what is $\\overset{―}{A\\cap B}?$",
      "worked_solution": "De Morgan's law for intersections states that\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{A\\cap B}≡\\overset{―}{A}\\cup \\overset{―}{B}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{A\\cap B} & =\\overset{―}{A}\\cup \\overset{―}{B} \\\\  & =\\{16,18,26\\}\\cup \\{10,16,25\\} \\\\  & =\\{10,16,18,25,26\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
