    "q-102573": {
      "dom_id": "step-q102573",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "If $\\overset{―}{A}=\\{\\sqrt{2},\\sqrt{7},\\sqrt{13}\\}$ and $\\overset{―}{B}=\\{\\sqrt{2},\\sqrt{5},\\sqrt{7},\\sqrt{11}\\},$ then what is $\\overset{―}{A\\cap B}?$",
      "worked_solution": "De Morgan's law for intersections states that\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{A\\cap B}≡\\overset{―}{A}\\cup \\overset{―}{B}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{A\\cap B} & =\\overset{―}{A}\\cup \\overset{―}{B} \\\\  & =\\{\\sqrt{2},\\sqrt{7},\\sqrt{13}\\}\\cup \\{\\sqrt{2},\\sqrt{5},\\sqrt{7},\\sqrt{11}\\} \\\\  & =\\{\\sqrt{2},\\sqrt{5},\\sqrt{7},\\sqrt{11},\\sqrt{13}\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
