      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "If $\\overset{―}{A}=\\{{a}_{2},{a}_{5},{a}_{7},{a}_{8}\\}$ and $\\overset{―}{B}=\\{{a}_{2},{a}_{4},{a}_{6},{a}_{8}\\},$ then what is $\\overset{―}{A\\cup B}?$",
      "worked_solution": "De Morgan's law for unions states that\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{A\\cup B}≡\\overset{―}{A}\\cap \\overset{―}{B}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{A\\cup B} & =\\overset{―}{A}\\cap \\overset{―}{B} \\\\  & =\\{{a}_{2},{a}_{5},{a}_{7},{a}_{8}\\}\\cap \\{{a}_{2},{a}_{4},{a}_{6},{a}_{8}\\} \\\\  & =\\{{a}_{2},{a}_{8}\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
